/-!
# Regularity of a Noetherian local filtered colimit

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 07DX
(blueprint: lem-per-noetherian-local-colimit-regular).

The theorem states that a filtered colimit of regular local rings with local transition maps
is regular local when its colimit ring is Noetherian. The indexing poset, transition maps,
and chosen categorical colimit are all represented directly by Mathlib's category-theoretic
interfaces.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace IsRegularLocalRing

/-- A Noetherian filtered colimit of regular local rings with local transition maps is regular
local. Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 07DX
(blueprint: lem-per-noetherian-local-colimit-regular).

Proof plan (the eight steps of the DAG node):
1. By lem-pc-filtered-colimit-commrings-elementwise, every colimit element has a stage
   representative and equality holds at a later stage. The images of stage maximal ideals
   form an ideal: move two representatives to a common stage for addition and multiplication.
   It is proper, since an equality between such a representative and one would hold at a later
   stage, contradicting properness there.
2. An element outside this ideal has a representative outside its stage maximal ideal and is
   a unit by lem-weil-pbc-local-ring-unit-criterion. Thus the colimit is local, with this unique
   maximal ideal. Its inverse image at each stage is the stage maximal ideal: an element
   outside the latter is a unit, and its image cannot lie in a proper ideal.
3. Each stage is a domain by lem-sc-regular-local-domain. Represent a zero product at a common
   stage, then move to a later stage where the product vanishes. One factor vanishes there,
   hence in the colimit. Properness in step 1 gives nontriviality; no injectivity is used.
4. Simultaneously for all such diagrams, induct strongly on the least generator number of
   the Noetherian colimit maximal ideal. At zero the colimit is a field of dimension zero.
   Otherwise take a minimal generating family x,x₂,...,xₙ. If x lay in the square of the
   maximal ideal, the other generators would span the cotangent space; Nakayama
   (lem-weil-pbc-nakayama-local-generators) would contradict minimality. In particular x ≠ 0.
5. Represent x at stage i, necessarily in its maximal ideal by step 2. At every j ≥ i its
   image xⱼ is outside the square, since membership would imply x lies in the colimit square.
   By lem-weil-pbc-regular-local-hypersurface-criterion, the quotients Lⱼ/(xⱼ) are regular
   local. The transition maps descend since they preserve these elements.
6. The tail has the same colimit: extend a cocone to a stage h through any common upper bound
   of h and i. Further upper bounds prove independence and compatibility. Maps from the
   quotient stages are exactly compatible stage maps killing xⱼ, so the colimit universal
   property (def-weil-pbc-category-colimit) identifies their colimit with L/(x).
7. The quotient of each local ring is local with the image maximal ideal: elements outside
   it lift to units. The same fact and locality of the original maps give local quotient
   maps. The quotient of L is Noetherian because ideal preimages are finitely generated
   (def-weil-pbc-noetherian-ring). Its maximal ideal is generated by the images of x₂,...,xₙ,
   so its minimal generator number is smaller. Apply strong induction to obtain regularity.
8. Step 3 and x ≠ 0 make x a nonzerodivisor. By
   lem-weil-pbc-dimension-quotient-nonzerodivisor, dim L = dim L/(x) + 1. Lift a minimal
   generating family of the regular quotient maximal ideal; together with x it generates
   the maximal ideal of L, with dim L elements. The regular-local definition in
   def-weil-regular-scheme concludes the proof. No assertion of locality of L is assumed.
-/
theorem of_noetherian_colimit {I : Type u} [PartialOrder I] [Nonempty I]
    [IsDirected I (· ≤ ·)] (F : I ⥤ CommRingCat.{u})
    [∀ i : I, IsRegularLocalRing (F.obj i)]
    (hlocal : ∀ (i j : I) (hij : i ≤ j),
      IsLocalHom (F.map (homOfLE hij)).hom)
    [IsNoetherianRing (colimit F : CommRingCat.{u})] :
    IsRegularLocalRing (colimit F : CommRingCat.{u}) := by
  sorry

end IsRegularLocalRing
